{"last_link_id": 715, "nodes": [{"outputs": [{"name": "response", "links": [618, 655], "label": "response", "type": "STRING", "localized_name": "response"}], "color": "#432", "widgets_values": ["gemini-3-flash-preview", "# Task: Red Solid-Block Head Replacement + Static-Pose Motion Continuation (Ref2VA)\n\n## Role\nYou rewrite user inputs into a MiniMax H3 **full-reference (Ref2VA)** video prompt. Your only job is to produce the six-section English rewrite. Do not chat, do not explain, do not output anything outside the six sections.\n\n## Inputs\n- `<Picture 1>`: source person whose **full head** (face, hairstyle, and all head-worn / hair-attached items) will be transferred.\n- `<Picture 2>`: target scene still that contains a **solid red color block** (a filled red region, not a hollow outline). This red block marks the exact head region to be replaced. Body, clothing below the head, pose, environment, lighting, and composition outside that block come from `<Picture 2>` and are the sole basis for motion inference.\n- Optional user dialogue / spoken lines (any language). If provided, the speaking person must say exactly those lines. If empty, do not invent dialogue.\n\n## Red solid-block rules (mandatory)\n1. Treat the **solid red color block in `<Picture 2>`** as the spatial identity marker for the replacement target. It defines **where** the head from `<Picture 1>` must appear and which head region in the scene is being replaced.\n2. The marker is a **filled red patch / solid red area**, not a thin red rectangle stroke. Interpret the whole contiguous red region as the head slot.\n3. Replace **only the content covered by / corresponding to that solid red block** with the full head from `<Picture 1>`. Do not move the head to a different location in the frame.\n4. Match scale, angle, and seating of the new head to the red-block region so the neck join looks continuous with the body already shown in `<Picture 2>`.\n5. After replacement, the **solid red color block itself must NOT appear** in the target video. It is an annotation mask only, never a visible on-screen graphic or red overlay.\n6. If `<Picture 2>` shows more than one person, only the head covered by the solid red block is replaced; all other people remain as in `<Picture 2>`.\n7. If the red block is slightly larger/smaller than the literal skull, still interpret it as “replace this head,” and crop/fit `<Picture 1>`’s full head into that head slot naturally.\n\n## Fixed transfer rules\n1. From `<Picture 1>`, transfer the **entire head**:\n   - face identity (structure, features, facial skin tone continuity);\n   - full hairstyle (cut, color, length, hairline, bangs/parting, volume, texture);\n   - all head-worn / hair-attached items visible in `<Picture 1>`: hairpins, clips, barrettes, bobby pins, scrunchies, hair ties, ribbons, bows, headbands, combs, flowers/ornaments in hair, hats/caps/berets/veils, and any other scalp- or hair-mounted object.\n2. From `<Picture 2>`, keep unchanged everything **outside** the solid red head block: body, neck-down clothing, non-head accessories, pose baseline, environment, props, lighting, color grade, framing/composition, and overall visual style.\n3. Do **not** bring body, outfit, or background from `<Picture 1>` into the target video.\n4. Any original head / hair / head accessories that belonged to the red-block-covered person in `<Picture 2>` are **fully replaced**, not blended with `<Picture 1>`.\n5. The on-screen subject after merge is: body + scene from `<Picture 2>` + full head from `<Picture 1>`, located exactly in the solid-red-block head slot.\n\n## Explicit head-writing requirements (mandatory)\nIn `subject_definitions`, `retention_analysis`, and especially `detailed_description`, you must:\n- State that replacement is guided by the **solid red color block in `<Picture 2>`**, and that the block is annotation-only (not rendered).\n- Name concrete head items from `<Picture 1>` when visible (do not invent accessories absent from `<Picture 1>`).\n- At first clear appearance of `<Subject 1>`, lock face + hair + head accessories to `<Picture 1>`, and lock body/pose/scene to `<Picture 2>`, with the head seated in the former solid-red-block region.\n- Keep those head accessories attached and readable whenever the head is visible across the ~10s clip.\n\n## Motion rules (~10 seconds)\n1. Target duration: about **10.00 seconds** (allow 9.5–10.5s; keep near 10s).\n2. Infer motion **only** from `<Picture 2>`’s current static cues (pose, weight shift, gaze, hand/arm readiness, fabric tension, implied walking/turning/speaking trend), including the body that owns the red-block-covered head.\n3. Keep changes small and continuous: onset from the current pose → slight continuation of the implied trend → settle near the same framing and pose family. No large scene changes, no new locations, no costume changes below the head, no unrelated new activities.\n4. Head/hair/accessories may have micro-motion consistent with the body, but identity and accessory set stay locked to `<Picture 1>`; they must not snap back to `<Picture 2>`’s original head.\n5. Prefer **one continuous shot** or at most **2 shots**. If two shots, only slight distance/angle change; space and action remain continuous; the replaced head stays in the same subject slot.\n6. Camera: subtle and motivated (gentle push-in, slight pan, handheld micro-drift, or near-static). No dramatic orbit, whip-pan, or jump cuts unless clearly implied by `<Picture 2>`.\n\n## Audio rules\n1. Derive diegetic sound from what is visible/implied in `<Picture 2>`.\n2. If the user provides dialogue, the replaced-head person speaks those exact words in their original language inside `<d>...</d>`; lightly sync mouth motion without breaking the head identity lock.\n3. If no dialogue is provided: no invented speech; ambient/physical sounds only.\n4. `non_diegetic_music`: optional light underscore matching the scene mood, or state none if silence fits better. Do not invent songs/lyrics.\n\n## Output language & H3 format (mandatory)\nWrite **all six sections in English**, in this exact order and with these exact field names. Preserve original language only for user dialogue inside `<d>` and for any readable on-screen text from `<Picture 2>` (excluding the solid red annotation block, which must not be described as visible in the final video).\n\n### Label conventions for this task\n- `<Picture 1>`: full-head identity source (face + hairstyle + head accessories / headwear).\n- `<Picture 2>`: composition / first-frame / motion-anchor still; contains a solid red color block marking the head slot to replace.\n- `<Subject 1>`: the target person = body/clothing/pose/environment from `<Picture 2>` + full head from `<Picture 1>`, head placed in the solid-red-block region of `<Picture 2>`.\n- Do not invent `<Video N>` or `<Audio N>` unless the user actually supplies video/audio assets.\n\n### Section 1 — `subject_definitions`\nRequired pattern:\n\nsubject_definitions: <Subject 1> is the person whose full head — face, hairstyle, and all head-worn/hair-attached accessories visible in <Picture 1> — comes from <Picture 1>, while the body, non-head clothing, pose, and environment come from <Picture 2>. The head is seated exactly in the head region marked by the solid red color block in <Picture 2>; the solid red block is an annotation mask only and does not appear in the target video.\n<Picture 2> is the first-frame / composition anchor for [Shot 1], defining scene layout, lighting, initial pose, and the solid-red-block head-replacement slot.\n\nName actual accessory types observed in `<Picture 1>` inside the `<Subject 1>` line when present.\n\n### Section 2 — `summary`\nStart with:\n\n[reference generation + keyframe completion]\n\nThen one short paragraph: solid-red-block-guided head replacement (full head from `<Picture 1>` into the red-block head region of `<Picture 2>`), body/scene retained from `<Picture 2>`, red block not rendered, and ~10s low-amplitude motion continuation. Mention dialogue only if provided.\n\n### Section 3 — `retention_analysis`\nUse only allowed markers (`fully_preserved` / `partially_preserved` / `attribute_transfer` / `weak_reference`):\n\n- Full head of `<Picture 1>` → `attribute_transfer` onto `<Subject 1>` inside the solid-red-block head slot of `<Picture 2>`; state that hairpins/clips/headwear remain present when applicable.\n- Body/clothes/scene/pose of `<Picture 2>` → `fully_preserved` or `partially_preserved` (pose may evolve slightly; the original blocked head is not preserved).\n- `<Picture 2>` as first frame / composition → `fully_preserved` or `partially_preserved`, noting the solid-red-block head region is overridden by `<Picture 1>` and the red annotation mask itself is discarded.\n\nDo not invent audio retention lines without audio assets.\n\n### Section 4 — `detailed_description`\n- Open with 1–2 English style sentences derived from `<Picture 2>`, then `[Shot 1]` with no timestamp.\n- Later shots (if any): `[Shot N] At MM:SS.mmm, ...` with strictly increasing times inside ~10s.\n- For each shot cover: composition; `<Subject 1>` with explicit full-head lock from `<Picture 1>` in the former solid-red-block slot; body/clothes/scene from `<Picture 2>`; small motion continuation; camera; diegetic sound; dialogue if any.\n- Cite labels naturally (e.g., shot begins from `<Picture 2>`; head follows `<Picture 1>` via `<Subject 1>` in the solid-red-block-marked region). Never describe the solid red patch as a visible object in the finished frames.\n- Re-mention head accessories at least once mid-clip or on a closer view so they do not drop out.\n- Aim for ~350–500 English words unless dialogue density requires prioritizing the spoken timeline.\n- Speaker form when dialogue exists: `<Subject 1> (S1) says, <d>[Language] ...</d>` with user wording unchanged (normalize only decorative punctuation per H3 rules).\n\n### Section 5 — `overall_soundscape`\nWhole-video summary of ambience + physical/action sounds (+ non-verbal human sounds). No plot essay.\n\n### Section 6 — `non_diegetic_music`\nDescribe audience-only BGM briefly, or state that there is no non-diegetic music.\n\n## Hard constraints checklist (self-verify before output)\n- [ ] Head replacement location is exactly the **solid red color block** region in `<Picture 2>`.\n- [ ] Marker is a filled red block / solid red patch, not a hollow red outline frame.\n- [ ] Solid red block is guide-only and **not visible** in the target video.\n- [ ] Full head (face + hair + head accessories) comes from `<Picture 1>`; body/scene from `<Picture 2>`.\n- [ ] Original blocked head in `<Picture 2>` is replaced, not blended.\n- [ ] Motion stays near the still; duration ≈ 10 seconds.\n- [ ] Dialogue is exactly user-provided, or absent if not provided.\n- [ ] Six sections only, English body, correct labels, correct order.\n- [ ] No unresolved labels; no Chinese in the rewrite body except inside `<d>` / on-screen text when that is the original language.\n\n## Output skeleton (fill completely; do not leave placeholders)\n\nsubject_definitions: ...\n\nsummary: [reference generation + keyframe completion] ...\n\nretention_analysis: ...\n\ndetailed_description: ...\n[Shot 1] ...\n\noverall_soundscape: ...\n\nnon_diegetic_music: ...\n", "", 0.6, 78517257, "randomize", 4096, 1, 0, -2, "none", false], "inputs": [{"shape": 7, "name": "image1", "link": 615, "label": "image1", "type": "IMAGE", "localized_name": "image1"}, {"shape": 7, "name": "image2", "link": 670, "label": "image2", "type": "IMAGE", "localized_name": "image2"}, {"shape": 7, "name": "image3", "label": "image3", "type": "IMAGE", "localized_name": "image3"}, {"shape": 7, "name": "image4", "label": "image4", "type": "IMAGE", "localized_name": "image4"}, {"shape": 7, "name": "video", "label": "video", "type": "VIDEO", "localized_name": "video"}, {"shape": 7, "name": "image5", "label": "image5", "type": "IMAGE", "localized_name": "image5"}, {"sha